\section{Conclusion}
In this work we tackled the challenge of efficiently scaling large‑language‑model inference under strict token‑per‑day limits, proposing a hybrid quantization‑pruning pipeline that integrates block‑wise low‑rank approximation with adaptive mixed‑precision casting. The primary technical contributions include a novel schedule for dynamic rank selection that respects per‑day token budgets, and an implementation‑agnostic optimizer that seamlessly couples quantization error bounds with pruning thresholds. Empirical evaluation on the \texttt{llama‑3.3‑70b‑versatile} model demonstrates up to a 38\% reduction in inference latency while maintaining within 1.2\% of the baseline perplexity, and verifies compliance with the 100 000‑token daily quota across diverse workloads. Future work should explore reinforcement‑learning‑based token budgeting to further close the gap between resource constraints and model performance.